#: ../../source/keyv_README.md:100
msgid "Third-party Storage Adapters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/keyv_README.md:102
msgid ""
"You can also use third-party storage adapters or build your own. Keyv "
"will wrap these storage adapters in TTL functionality and handle complex "
"types internally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/keyv_README.md:111
msgid ""
"Any store that follows the [`Map`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-"
"US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Map) api will work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/keyv_README.md:117
msgid ""
"For example, [`quick-lru`](https://github.com/sindresorhus/quick-lru) is "
"a completely unrelated module that implements the Map API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/keyv_README.md:127
msgid "Add Cache Support to your Module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/keyv_README.md:129
msgid ""
"Keyv is designed to be easily embedded into other modules to add cache "
"support. The recommended pattern is to expose a `cache` option in your "
"modules options which is passed through to Keyv. Caching will work in "
"memory by default and users have the option to also install a Keyv "
"storage adapter and pass in a connection string, or any other storage "
"that implements the `Map` API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/keyv_README.md:131
msgid ""
"You should also set a namespace for your module so you can safely call "
"`.clear()` without clearing unrelated app data."
msgstr ""

